The Nautilus DevOps team is strategizing the migration of a portion of their infrastructure to the AWS cloud. 
Recognizing the scale of this undertaking, they have opted to approach the migration in incremental steps rather than as a single massive transition. 
To achieve this, they have segmented large tasks into smaller, more manageable units.

For this task, create an EC2 instance using Terraform with the following requirements:

The EC2 instance must use the value datacenter-ec2 as its Name tag, which defines the instance name in AWS.

Use the Amazon Linux ami-0c101f26f147fa7fd to launch this instance.

The Instance type must be t2.micro.

Create a new RSA key named datacenter-kp.

Attach the default (available by default) security group.

The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform. Create the main.tf file (do not create a different .tf file) to provision the instance.

Note: Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.

SOLUTION
To create the EC2 instance with all the specified requirements, you'll need to generate an RSA key pair and then reference the default security group. Here is the content for your /home/bob/terraform/main.tf file:

hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

# Generate a new RSA private key
resource "tls_private_key" "datacenter_kp" {
  algorithm = "RSA"
  rsa_bits  = 4096
}

# Create the AWS key pair using the generated public key
resource "aws_key_pair" "datacenter_kp" {
  key_name   = "datacenter-kp"
  public_key = tls_private_key.datacenter_kp.public_key_openssh
}

# Reference the default security group in the default VPC
data "aws_security_group" "default" {
  name = "default"
}

# Create the EC2 instance
resource "aws_instance" "datacenter_ec2" {
  ami                    = "ami-0c101f26f147fa7fd"
  instance_type          = "t2.micro"
  key_name               = aws_key_pair.datacenter_kp.key_name
  vpc_security_group_ids = [data.aws_security_group.default.id]

  tags = {
    Name = "datacenter-ec2"
  }
}
💡 Key Details
RSA Key Pair: The tls_private_key resource generates a new RSA key locally, and aws_key_pair uploads its public portion to AWS with the name datacenter-kp .

Default Security Group: The data "aws_security_group" "default" block looks up the existing default security group by name, so you can attach it without modifying it .

Instance Configuration: The AMI, instance type, and Name tag are set exactly as specified in the task.

🚀 Execution Steps
Run the following in the terminal inside /home/bob/terraform:

bash
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
